  "reason": "Evidence: All five completed experiments are singleprofile. PCA_n2000 clearly outperforms scgpt as RNA encoder (0.523 vs 0.421), and concat fusion marginally beats weighted (0.527 vs 0.523) with pca_n2000+resnet50. RNA dominates over image (0.485 vs 0.208), and multimodal adds ~4 pts over RNA alone. The largest unexplored design axis is multiprofile aggregation—no multiprofile experiment has been run yet. Question: Does aggregating multiple profiles (via avgpool) on top of our best singleprofile settings (pca_n2000, resnet50, concat) improve validation accuracy, or does it dilute the signal? Why this experiment: config_008 is the minimal, direct extension of our best result (config_041) by adding only the multiprofile+avgpool aggregation step, isolating that single design choice. Avgpool is the simpler aggregation; if it fails to help, a more complex transformer aggregation is less likely to. This single experiment resolves whether the multiprofile axis is worth further investment under our limited budget."
}

